[111.597885, "o", "\u001b[33mhint: Using 'master' as the name for the initial branch. This default branch name\u001b[m"]
[111.598366, "o", "\r\n"]
[111.59859, "o", "\u001b[33mhint: will change to \"main\" in Git 3.0. To configure the initial branch name\u001b[m"]
[111.599156, "o", "\r\n"]
[111.599376, "o", "\u001b[33mhint: to use in all of your new repositories, which will suppress this warning,\u001b[m"]
[111.599608, "o", "\r\n"]
[111.599864, "o", "\u001b[33mhint: call:\u001b[m"]
[111.600134, "o", "\r\n"]
[111.600356, "o", "\u001b[33mhint:\u001b[m"]
[111.600581, "o", "\r\n"]
[111.600841, "o", "\u001b[33mhint: "]
[111.601058, "o", "\t"]
[111.601274, "o", "git config --global init.defaultBranch <name>\u001b[m"]
[111.602323, "o", "\r\n"]
[111.602942, "o", "\u001b[33mhint:\u001b[m"]
[111.603295, "o", "\r\n"]
[111.603518, "o", "\u001b[33mhint: Names commonly chosen instead of 'master' are 'main', 'trunk' and\u001b[m"]
[111.603816, "o", "\r\n"]
[111.604164, "o", "\u001b[33mhint: 'development'. The just-created branch can be renamed via this command:\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[33mhint:\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[33mhint: \tgit branch -m <name>\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[33mhint:\u001b[m"]
[111.604353, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33mhint: Disable this message with \"git config set advice.defaultBranchName false\"\u001b[m\r\n"]
[111.606806, "o", "Initialized empty Git repository in /git/project/\r\n"]
